Supporting materials for the ACL2 Workshop 2026 paper

  Pablo Oscar Cayuela
  Mechanized Verification of Complex-to-Vector Derivations in a
  Three-Phase AC Machine Model

Mechanical verification, in ACL2 and ACL2(r), of the algebraic
derivations of a vectorial model of the symmetric three-phase AC
machine, including a sign correction in the torque equation.

Books (one per section of the paper; see also the repository
https://github.com/pcayuela/ACL2-ACmotormodel-check):

  00-complex-vectors.lisp        complex numbers as pairs; dot/cross products
  01-euler-identities.lisp       Euler identities (encapsulated cosine/sine)
  02-roots-of-unity.lisp         cube roots of unity
  03-zeta-deduction.lisp         space-vector angle
  04-collapse-lemma.lisp         three-phase collapse lemma
  05-torque-sign-correction.lisp torque exponent sign
  06-generic-omega-collapse.lisp          generic collapse lemma (conditional)
  06-generic-omega-collapse-acl2r.lisp    ... made unconditional (ACL2(r))
  07-inductance-note.lisp        note on the air-gap integral
  08-inductance-integral.lisp    progress on the integral (ACL2(r))
  09-nonvacuity-acl2r.lisp       the s3^2=3 hypothesis is satisfiable in
                                 ACL2(r); trig constraints hold for
                                 acl2-cosine/acl2-sine (ACL2(r))

Top books:
  top.lisp                    00-07 (ACL2; also certifies under ACL2(r))
  top-acl2r.lisp              06-...-acl2r and 08 (requires ACL2(r))
  top-acl2r-nonvacuity.lisp   09, and hence 00-05 (requires ACL2(r))

Books marked "cert_param: (uses-acl2r)" are certified only with the
ACL2(r) executable.
